+- [ ] T-1283 [P2] Receipt storage is O(N) in lifetime volume on the read path and O(N squared) cumulatively on the append path, and the project has already crossed into multi-second routine commands. Measured live: 2592 settled receipt directories with a settled index holding 1567 entries and therefore stale, semantic_receipts_for_operation_safe returning 2 matches in 5.75s at 43.5 MiB, sub_list at 6.35s, and one latest_receipt core call invoking the per-receipt content hash 1052 times over 1052 conformance receipts. Two distinct causes were separated during the SRC-018 audit work. First, the settled index cannot self-heal, and the reason is deeper than the branch the audit named: instrumented, the settlement-time bootstrap RUNS and succeeds and the index it writes still fails validation immediately, because the digest is taken before the operation record is final, so the repair belongs in the journal commit sequencing rather than in the branch. Second, the conformance lineage validates a direct locator by hashing the entire historical receipt population on every lookup and re-hashes the full membership on every append. The audit prescribes bounded immutable sealed segments with a small append-active tail for both stores | verify: AC-01 a settlement leaves a settled index that validates on the next read, proven by a test that goes red against the current sequencing; AC-02 an operation-specific query consults the index or segment offsets and does not construct a full semantic snapshot, proven by counting decodes rather than by timing; AC-03 latest_receipt validates its locator against a compact lineage generation and the per-receipt content-hash count stops scaling with the population, proven by the PERF-004 measurement control already in place; AC-04 an append inside the active segment does not re-hash sealed segments; AC-05 exact-byte receipt evidence stays authoritative and a deep leaf-by-leaf audit remains reachable from the explicit validation path; AC-06 red controls prove each new bound can go red; unittest, audit_checks and ruff PASS
